IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cla-dates`
IMPORT `cla-core`
IMPORT `cla-seat`

-- Civil Liability Act 1936 (SA) -- cases for the claimant's seat (cla-seat.l4), with a few on cla-core.l4 functions
-- the seat does not reach (the 2002 and 2003 amounts). Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text
-- (the section is named on each group), never copied from the encoding's output. Edges: the last day of the three
-- years and of the six months (leap years and month ends), 27, 28 and 29 November 1974, 30 April and 1 May 2004,
-- 30 June and 1 July 2013 and 2014, every band edge of s 52(3)(c), injury scale values 7/8 and 10/11 and reg 7
-- rounding, the half-way $5 in rounding, blood alcohol .08 and .15, age 15 and 16, the prescribed minimum and maximum.
-- CPI figures are invented test figures, not the ABS series.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases: the claimant`

`MVA` MEANS `in an MVA motor accident`
`train` MEANS `in another motor accident`
`negligence` MEANS `in an accident caused wholly or partly by negligence, another person's unintentional tort, or a breach of a contractual duty of care`
`other way` MEANS `in some other way`
`family` MEANS `your parent, spouse, domestic partner or child`

§§ `s 24(1), (5): for whose benefit`

#ASSERT `Is the death action brought for my benefit` `a child, grandchild or step-child` FALSE EQUALS `yes: the action for the death is brought for your benefit (s 24(1))`
#ASSERT `Is the death action brought for my benefit` `a brother or sister, including a half- or step-brother or sister` FALSE EQUALS `yes: the action for the death is brought for your benefit (s 24(1))`
#ASSERT `Is the death action brought for my benefit` `a grandparent or step-parent` FALSE EQUALS `yes: the action for the death is brought for your benefit (s 24(1))`
#ASSERT `Is the death action brought for my benefit` `the domestic partner` TRUE EQUALS `the action need not be brought for your benefit: you renounced it by written notice served on the executor or administrator (s 24(5))`
#ASSERT `Is the death action brought for my benefit` `none of these` FALSE EQUALS `no: the action is for the spouse, domestic partner, parent, brother, sister and child of the deceased only (s 24(1))`

§§ `ss 24(1), 25, 27(1): who may bring it (death 31 August 2023; six months end 29 February 2024)`

#ASSERT `May I bring the death action myself` `the spouse` FALSE FALSE (`the date` 31 8 2023) (`the date` 1 9 2023) EQUALS `you may bring it yourself: there is no executor or administrator (s 27(1))`
#ASSERT `May I bring the death action myself` `the spouse` TRUE FALSE (`the date` 31 8 2023) (`the date` 29 2 2024) EQUALS `not yet: the executor or administrator brings it (s 24(1)); you may bring it yourself only if none is commenced within six months after the death (s 27(1))`
#ASSERT `May I bring the death action myself` `the spouse` TRUE FALSE (`the date` 31 8 2023) (`the date` 1 3 2024) EQUALS `you may bring it yourself: no action under Part 5 was commenced within six months after the death (s 27(1))`
#ASSERT `May I bring the death action myself` `the spouse` TRUE TRUE (`the date` 31 8 2023) (`the date` 1 3 2024) EQUALS `no: not more than one action lies under Part 5 for the same subject matter, and one has been commenced (s 25)`
#ASSERT `May I bring the death action myself` `none of these` FALSE FALSE (`the date` 31 8 2023) (`the date` 1 3 2024) EQUALS `no: you are not a person for whose benefit the action could be brought (ss 24(1), 27(1))`

§§ `s 25: within three years after the death`

#ASSERT `By when must the death action be commenced` (`the date` 15 3 2022) EQUALS `the date` 15 3 2025
#ASSERT `By when must the death action be commenced` (`the date` 29 2 2024) EQUALS `the date` 28 2 2027
#ASSERT `Was the death action commenced in time` (`the date` 15 3 2022) TRUE (`the date` 15 3 2025) (`the date` 1 6 2025) EQUALS `in time: it was commenced within three years after the death`
#ASSERT `Was the death action commenced in time` (`the date` 15 3 2022) TRUE (`the date` 16 3 2025) (`the date` 1 6 2025) EQUALS `out of time: it was not commenced within three years after the death`
#ASSERT `Was the death action commenced in time` (`the date` 15 3 2022) FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2000) (`the date` 15 3 2025) EQUALS `still in time: the three years after the death have not yet run out`
#ASSERT `Was the death action commenced in time` (`the date` 15 3 2022) FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2000) (`the date` 16 3 2025) EQUALS `out of time: it was not commenced within three years after the death`
#ASSERT `Was the death action commenced in time` (`the date` 29 2 2024) TRUE (`the date` 28 2 2027) (`the date` 1 6 2027) EQUALS `in time: it was commenced within three years after the death`
#ASSERT `Was the death action commenced in time` (`the date` 29 2 2024) TRUE (`the date` 1 3 2027) (`the date` 1 6 2027) EQUALS `out of time: it was not commenced within three years after the death`

§§ `s 24(2a), (2aa): what the damages for a death count`

#ASSERT `Is this payment deducted from the damages for the death` `superannuation payments or benefits because of the death` EQUALS `no: it is not taken into account in assessing the damages for the death (s 24(2aa))`
#ASSERT `Is this payment deducted from the damages for the death` `a sum under a contract of life assurance or insurance` EQUALS `no: it is not taken into account in assessing the damages for the death (s 24(2aa))`
#ASSERT `Is this payment deducted from the damages for the death` `another payment` EQUALS `s 24(2aa) does not exclude it: whether it is taken into account is left to the general law`
#ASSERT `Can the death damages include medical and funeral expenses` TRUE EQUALS `yes: damages may be awarded for the medical expenses of the injury that caused the death and the funeral expenses (s 24(2a))`
#ASSERT `Can the death damages include medical and funeral expenses` FALSE EQUALS `no: s 24(2a) covers only medical and funeral expenses incurred by the persons for whose benefit the action is brought`

§§ `ss 28-30: solatium`

#ASSERT `What solatium can I get for my child's death` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`the date` 1 1 2020) FALSE EQUALS `yes: the court may award the sum it thinks just, up to` 10000
#ASSERT `What solatium can I get for my child's death` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`the date` 27 11 1974) FALSE EQUALS `yes: the court may award the sum it thinks just, up to` 1000
#ASSERT `What solatium can I get for my child's death` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`the date` 28 11 1974) FALSE EQUALS `the Act sets no maximum for a death on 28 November 1974, the day the 1974 amendments commenced (ss 28(1), 29(1))`
#ASSERT `What solatium can I get for my child's death` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`the date` 29 11 1974) FALSE EQUALS `yes: the court may award the sum it thinks just, up to` 10000
#ASSERT `What solatium can I get for my child's death` FALSE TRUE TRUE (`the date` 1 1 2020) FALSE EQUALS `no: solatium under s 28 is for the father or mother of a child who was an infant (s 28(1), (4))`
#ASSERT `What solatium can I get for my child's death` TRUE FALSE TRUE (`the date` 1 1 2020) FALSE EQUALS `no: solatium under s 28 is for the father or mother of a child who was an infant (s 28(1), (4))`
#ASSERT `What solatium can I get for my child's death` TRUE TRUE FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2020) FALSE EQUALS `no: the death was not caused by a wrongful act, neglect or default that would have entitled the deceased to sue (ss 28(1), 29(1))`
#ASSERT `What solatium can I get for my child's death` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`the date` 1 1 2020) TRUE EQUALS `no: the court has refused it, having regard to your conduct or relations with the deceased or another sufficient reason (s 30(2))`
#ASSERT `What solatium can I get for my partner's death` `the spouse` TRUE (`the date` 1 1 2020) FALSE EQUALS `yes: the court may award the sum it thinks just, up to` 10000
#ASSERT `What solatium can I get for my partner's death` `the domestic partner` TRUE (`the date` 1 1 2020) FALSE EQUALS `yes: the court may award the sum it thinks just, up to` 10000
#ASSERT `What solatium can I get for my partner's death` `the spouse` TRUE (`the date` 27 11 1974) FALSE EQUALS `yes: the court may award the sum it thinks just, up to` 1400
#ASSERT `What solatium can I get for my partner's death` `the father or mother` TRUE (`the date` 1 1 2020) FALSE EQUALS `no: solatium under s 29 is for the surviving spouse or domestic partner (s 29(1))`

§§ `ss 37-39: obvious and inherent risks`

#ASSERT `Am I taken to have known of the obvious risk` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `you are taken to have been aware of the risk (s 37(1)); the defence may then succeed`
#ASSERT `Am I taken to have known of the obvious risk` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `you are not taken to have been aware of it: you proved you were not actually aware of the risk (s 37(1))`
#ASSERT `Am I taken to have known of the obvious risk` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: the defence fails, because a reasonable person in your position would not have taken steps to avoid the risk (s 37(3))`
#ASSERT `Am I taken to have known of the obvious risk` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `s 37(1) does not apply: the risk was not an obvious risk, so your awareness is left to the general law`
#ASSERT `Am I taken to have known of the obvious risk` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `s 37 does not apply: the defendant has not raised voluntary assumption of risk`
#ASSERT `Did they have to warn me of the obvious risk` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: there is no duty to warn you of an obvious risk (s 38(1))`
#ASSERT `Did they have to warn me of the obvious risk` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 38(1) does not apply, but that raises no presumption of a duty to warn; the general law decides (s 38(2), (3))`
#ASSERT `Did they have to warn me of the obvious risk` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `s 38(1) does not apply, but that raises no presumption of a duty to warn; the general law decides (s 38(2), (3))`
#ASSERT `Did they have to warn me of the obvious risk` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 38 does not deal with a risk that was not obvious`
#ASSERT `Can I sue for an inherent risk` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: there is no liability in negligence for harm from the materialisation of an inherent risk (s 39(1))`
#ASSERT `Can I sue for an inherent risk` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `s 39 does not exclude liability for failing to warn of the risk (s 39(3))`
#ASSERT `Can I sue for an inherent risk` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 39 does not apply: the risk could have been avoided by reasonable care and skill`

§§ `s 43: criminal conduct`

#ASSERT `Is my claim excluded for criminal conduct` `MVA` `you were convicted of the offence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: your claim for damages is excluded, because the accident happened while you were committing an indictable offence that contributed materially to the risk of injury (s 43(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my claim excluded for criminal conduct` `negligence` `no conviction or acquittal, and the court is satisfied beyond reasonable doubt that you were committing it` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: your claim for damages is excluded, because the accident happened while you were committing an indictable offence that contributed materially to the risk of injury (s 43(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my claim excluded for criminal conduct` `MVA` `you were convicted of the offence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the exclusion applies, but the court may still award damages because the case is exceptional and the exclusion would operate harshly and unjustly (s 43(2))`
#ASSERT `Is my claim excluded for criminal conduct` `MVA` `you were acquitted of the offence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `s 43 does not exclude your claim`
#ASSERT `Is my claim excluded for criminal conduct` `MVA` `you were convicted of the offence` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 43 does not exclude your claim`
#ASSERT `Is my claim excluded for criminal conduct` `other way` `you were convicted of the offence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `s 43 does not apply to how the injury arose (s 43(4))`

§§ `s 46: your own intoxication (with s 48)`

#ASSERT `Are my damages reduced for my intoxication` 0.08 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `contributory negligence is presumed, and your damages are reduced by at least` 25
#ASSERT `Are my damages reduced for my intoxication` 0.079 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 46 raises no presumption: you were not intoxicated, or the defendant does not allege contributory negligence`
#ASSERT `Are my damages reduced for my intoxication` 0.15 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `contributory negligence is presumed, and your damages are reduced by at least` 50
#ASSERT `Are my damages reduced for my intoxication` 0.149 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `contributory negligence is presumed, and your damages are reduced by at least` 25
#ASSERT `Are my damages reduced for my intoxication` 0.15 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `contributory negligence is presumed, and your damages are reduced by at least` 25
#ASSERT `Are my damages reduced for my intoxication` 0 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `contributory negligence is presumed, and your damages are reduced by at least` 50
#ASSERT `Are my damages reduced for my intoxication` 0.2 FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the presumption is rebutted (s 46(2)); an ordinary finding of contributory negligence is still possible`
#ASSERT `Are my damages reduced for my intoxication` 0.2 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the presumption is rebutted (s 46(2)); an ordinary finding of contributory negligence is still possible`
#ASSERT `Are my damages reduced for my intoxication` 0.2 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `s 46 raises no presumption: you were not intoxicated, or the defendant does not allege contributory negligence`

