§§ `ss 56, 57: interest and management`

#ASSERT `Can I get interest on this part of my damages` `non-economic loss` EQUALS `no: interest is not awarded on damages for non-economic or future loss (s 56)`
#ASSERT `Can I get interest on this part of my damages` `future loss` EQUALS `no: interest is not awarded on damages for non-economic or future loss (s 56)`
#ASSERT `Can I get interest on this part of my damages` `past economic loss` EQUALS `ss 56 and 57 do not exclude interest on damages for past economic loss`
#ASSERT `Can I get interest on this part of my damages` `the cost of investing or managing the award` EQUALS `no: damages are not awarded for the cost of investing or managing the amount awarded (s 57)`

§§ `ss 58, 58A, reg 19: gratuitous services`

#ASSERT `Can I get damages for my family's care` `negligence` (`the date` 1 6 2015) `family` 0 2 1 FALSE FALSE 1800 EQUALS `yes: damages for the services, up to 4 times State average weekly earnings, that is` 7200
#ASSERT `Can I get damages for my family's care` `negligence` (`the date` 1 6 2015) `family` 0 2 1 FALSE TRUE 1800 EQUALS `yes: damages for the services above 4 times State average weekly earnings, at a rate no higher than State average weekly earnings, that is per week at most` 1800
#ASSERT `Can I get damages for my family's care` `negligence` (`the date` 1 6 2015) `someone else` 0 2 1 FALSE FALSE 1800 EQUALS `no: damages are not awarded for gratuitous services except those of a parent, spouse, domestic partner or child (s 58(1)(a))`
#ASSERT `Can I get damages for my family's care` `MVA` (`the date` 1 6 2020) `family` 11 6 6 FALSE FALSE 1800 EQUALS `yes: damages for the services, up to 4 times State average weekly earnings, that is` 7200
#ASSERT `Can I get damages for my family's care` `MVA` (`the date` 1 6 2020) `family` 10 6 6 FALSE FALSE 1800 EQUALS `no: after an MVA motor accident, the injury scale value must exceed 10 and the services be given for at least 6 hours a week for at least 6 consecutive months (s 58(4)(a))`
#ASSERT `Can I get damages for my family's care` `MVA` (`the date` 1 6 2020) `family` 11 5.9 6 FALSE FALSE 1800 EQUALS `no: after an MVA motor accident, the injury scale value must exceed 10 and the services be given for at least 6 hours a week for at least 6 consecutive months (s 58(4)(a))`
#ASSERT `Can I get damages for my family's care` `MVA` (`the date` 1 6 2020) `family` 11 6 5 FALSE FALSE 1800 EQUALS `no: after an MVA motor accident, the injury scale value must exceed 10 and the services be given for at least 6 hours a week for at least 6 consecutive months (s 58(4)(a))`
#ASSERT `Can I get damages for my family's care` `MVA` (`the date` 1 6 2020) `family` 30 20 12 TRUE FALSE 1800 EQUALS `no: as a Lifetime Support Scheme participant, not for services meeting your assessed treatment, care and support needs from the injury (s 58(5))`
#ASSERT `Can I get damages for my family's care` `MVA` (`the date` 30 6 2013) `family` 0 2 1 FALSE FALSE 1800 EQUALS `yes: damages for the services, up to 4 times State average weekly earnings, that is` 7200
#ASSERT `What is the highest hourly rate for family care` (`the date` 1 1 2014) 116.6 102.4 EQUALS 25
#ASSERT `What is the highest hourly rate for family care` (`the date` 1 9 2020) 116.6 102.4 EQUALS 28.466796875
#ASSERT `Can a scheme participant get damages for care needs` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: no damages for treatment, care and support needs from the injury that arise while you are a participant in the Lifetime Support Scheme (s 58A)`
#ASSERT `Can a scheme participant get damages for care needs` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `s 58A does not bar these damages`

§§ `s 65: consortium`

#ASSERT `Can I claim for loss of consortium` TRUE TRUE `negligence` (`the date` 1 6 2020) 0 EQUALS `yes: the wrongdoer is liable to you for the loss or impairment of consortium (s 65(1))`
#ASSERT `Can I claim for loss of consortium` TRUE TRUE `MVA` (`the date` 1 6 2020) 10 EQUALS `no: after an MVA motor accident, damages for loss of consortium need an injury scale value over 10 (s 65(2))`
#ASSERT `Can I claim for loss of consortium` TRUE TRUE `MVA` (`the date` 1 6 2020) 11 EQUALS `yes: the wrongdoer is liable to you for the loss or impairment of consortium (s 65(1))`
#ASSERT `Can I claim for loss of consortium` FALSE TRUE `MVA` (`the date` 1 6 2020) 11 EQUALS `no: s 65 is for the spouse or domestic partner of the injured person`
#ASSERT `Can I claim for loss of consortium` TRUE FALSE `MVA` (`the date` 1 6 2020) 11 EQUALS `no: s 65 needs an injury caused by a wrongful act, neglect or default`

§§ `s 67: the costs of raising a child`

#ASSERT `Can I get damages for raising the child` `negligence resulting in the unintended conception of a child` FALSE EQUALS `no: no damages for the ordinary costs of raising the child (s 67(1))`
#ASSERT `Can I get damages for raising the child` `breach of warranty of merchantable quality or fitness for purpose of a contraceptive device that failed` TRUE EQUALS `no damages for the ordinary costs of raising the child (s 67(1)); the costs by which the child's disability reasonably increases them are not ordinary costs (s 67(2))`
#ASSERT `Can I get damages for raising the child` `another kind of action` FALSE EQUALS `s 67 does not apply to this kind of action (s 67(3))`

§§ `s 70: damages for unreasonable delay (death 10 March 2003; three years end 10 March 2006)`

#ASSERT `Can I claim damages for unreasonable delay` (`the date` 10 3 2003) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (`the date` 10 3 2006) (`the date` 1 6 2006) EQUALS `yes: exemplary damages may be awarded against the person in default (s 70(1), (2)); paid to the dependants unless there are none or there is another good reason (s 70(7), (8))`
#ASSERT `Can I claim damages for unreasonable delay` (`the date` 10 3 2003) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (`the date` 11 3 2006) (`the date` 1 6 2006) EQUALS `no: the claim was not brought within 3 years after the death (s 70(4))`
#ASSERT `Can I claim damages for unreasonable delay` (`the date` 10 3 2003) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2000) (`the date` 1 1 2006) EQUALS `yes: exemplary damages may be awarded against the person in default (s 70(1), (2)); paid to the dependants unless there are none or there is another good reason (s 70(7), (8))`
#ASSERT `Can I claim damages for unreasonable delay` (`the date` 9 3 2003) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (`the date` 10 3 2005) (`the date` 1 6 2005) EQUALS `no: s 70 applies only where the deceased died on or after 10 March 2003 (s 70(9))`
#ASSERT `Can I claim damages for unreasonable delay` (`the date` 1 6 2020) TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (`the date` 1 6 2021) (`the date` 1 7 2021) EQUALS `no: the conditions in s 70(2) are not all met`
#ASSERT `By when must the delay claim be brought` (`the date` 10 3 2003) EQUALS `the date` 10 3 2006

§§ `ss 74, 75: good samaritans and apologies`

#ASSERT `Can I sue the good samaritan` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: a good samaritan incurs no personal civil liability for what was done in good faith and without recklessness (s 74(2))`
#ASSERT `Can I sue the good samaritan` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 74 gives no immunity on these facts`
#ASSERT `Can I sue the good samaritan` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: a medically qualified good samaritan incurs no personal civil liability for advice about emergency medical assistance (s 74(3))`
#ASSERT `Can I sue the good samaritan` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the immunity does not extend to a liability within compulsory third party motor vehicle insurance (s 74(4)(a))`
#ASSERT `Can I sue the good samaritan` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the immunity does not operate: their capacity was significantly impaired by alcohol or another recreational drug (s 74(4)(b))`
#ASSERT `Can I sue the good samaritan` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 74 gives no immunity on these facts`
#ASSERT `Does their apology count as an admission` FALSE EQUALS `no: the apology is not an admission of fault or liability, is not relevant to it, and is not admissible as evidence of it (s 75(1), (2))`
#ASSERT `Does their apology count as an admission` TRUE EQUALS `s 75 does not apply to a defamation claim (s 75(3)(a))`
